# Stone's pinned apps: each line bundles one app module in Stone's build.
# scripts/fetch-apps.sh downloads the module and its release inventory,
# and stops the build unless the module's SHA-256 matches the pin and the
# inventory lists that same SHA-256 for app.wasm and the pinned check-in.
# The pin, in Stone's own history, is the guard; the inventory confirms it.
# Plan: stone forum df2aca7b58 step 2; route 1 in ollama docs/release-flow.md.
#
# Fields, separated by spaces:
#   name       the app's name, lowercase letters, digits and dashes
#   project    its project (repository name)
#   check-in   the full source check-in hash the release was built from
#   sha256     the expected SHA-256 of app.wasm
#   module     HTTPS address of app.wasm
#   inventory  HTTPS address of the release's file list (release.txt)
#
# The download addresses and access are still to be agreed with OCX, so
# no app is pinned yet. Hello stays in ios/Stone/Apps/hello, in source.
